On 09/22/2011 09:15 AM, Kathryn Iverson wrote:
> Hi Gord,
> Thanks for the information, although I'm not quite sure how to proceed.
> My understanding is I need to compile a shared library libbam and put it in
> /usr/local/lib64. Is the source for this library in Rsamtools itself? I've
> untared Rsamtools and am looking around for some kind of makefile but can't
> seem to find it. I see something in src/Makvars but there is no target for
> dylib.


As a workaround I *think* you can edit src/Makevars.common to read

PKG_LIBS += \
   $(SHLIB_OPENMP_CFLAGS) \
   -Llibbam.a -Llibbcf.a -Llibtabix.a

instead of

PKG_LIBS += \
   $(SHLIB_OPENMP_CFLAGS) \
   -L. -lbam -lbcf -ltabix

Martin

